                  <provenance type="#s c"><orgName role="fmo" key="mlgbOrg_295">Lanthony (secunda),
                        Gloucestershire. Augustinian priory of St Mary the Virgin and St John the
                        Baptist</orgName><p>Contains at end 'Nomina fundatorum ecclesie beate
                        marie lanthon' extra Gloucestr' defunctorum et in domo capitulari ibidem
                        quiescentum' (s. xv) and, at beginning, a list of constables of England from
                        1067, including references to Lanthony (s. xiv).</p></provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">Given to John Anstis by Richard Graves of
                     Mickleton, Glos. MS number 10 at the Blyke sale, 11 May 1776 (v. cat. p. 114).
                     Possibly lot 94 in the G. Scott sale, 12 March 1781. Given to Bristol Baptist
                     College by Andrew Gifford (d. 1784). At the location, described by Ker, MMBL,
                     2. 190-91. Later sold and recorded in Supplement as in a private
                     collection.</provenance>
